                                                "text": "I am also disappointed with the horses, having hardly seen a decent pair yet, while the traps and horses do not look smart and well groomed. There are a great many American spiders used. Have not seen a bullock in the yoke yet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fee7306-5cf6-33a1-be87-a234f530f652",
                                        "entry_id": "f73d8d49-333c-3d8d-8c9d-eed8626570d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A support for a camera tripod, preventing it from sliding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75900b08-107d-479e-8df5-edf7a1f7ee96",
                                                "sense_id": "6fee7306-5cf6-33a1-be87-a234f530f652",
                                                "text": "The spider is very useful for shooting in the studio or on locations with smooth floors where tripod legs tend to slide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "156905fc-9dc6-3032-873e-dbc91420c31f",
                                        "entry_id": "f73d8d49-333c-3d8d-8c9d-eed8626570d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A competition in which several participants are spread evenly around the edges of the green, who all make one bowl towards the central jack at the same time; the winner being the person whose bowl ends up closest to the jack."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spider",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90f9238d-4f14-398e-912b-446d6cf6c5ec",
                                        "entry_id": "c393ae0c-c797-3354-a371-205ed7f8db63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move like a spider."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0aecd284-3790-4a57-b4e9-65ccda6b1378",
                                                "sense_id": "90f9238d-4f14-398e-912b-446d6cf6c5ec",
                                                "text": "A year later she returned to El Cap and spidered up the wall again — this time in 23 hours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5158d6b4-acfd-400c-ae1d-4d33ab0dd50a",
                                                "sense_id": "90f9238d-4f14-398e-912b-446d6cf6c5ec",
                                                "text": "They saved the hall though the facing and part of the roof had to be torn out and replaced, men spidered over the building to repair it before Coaker's arrival."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a343f1a-13df-4517-8194-25105439b69a",
                                                "sense_id": "90f9238d-4f14-398e-912b-446d6cf6c5ec",
                                                "text": "Briefly he considered letting go to glide along in Radu's wake as the assassin spidered up the wall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54ad5e55-93aa-344f-a73e-47c57fcb8733",
                                        "entry_id": "c393ae0c-c797-3354-a371-205ed7f8db63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cover a surface like a cobweb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "134f76fc-541d-4d05-a88d-6edf34fa79f4",
                                                "sense_id": "54ad5e55-93aa-344f-a73e-47c57fcb8733",
                                                "text": "High walls surrounded it on all sides, each one covered with the skeletal stems of climbing plants that spidered across the stones, and the ground was cobbled between patches of frozen grass."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6cde4f4-2769-424b-be99-6b7e0cdff982",
                                                "sense_id": "54ad5e55-93aa-344f-a73e-47c57fcb8733",
                                                "text": "Large cracks spidered across the mask's glass where the nozzle had hit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2b9b6ad-d42c-4afe-9650-383bca36fbe9",
                                                "sense_id": "54ad5e55-93aa-344f-a73e-47c57fcb8733",
                                                "text": "Moss spidered across the stone, fresh green. Seaweed sprouted bright yellows and ochres between the vast webs of fingers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a520a41d-ff81-3b11-8da4-ecdf877e7935",
                                        "entry_id": "c393ae0c-c797-3354-a371-205ed7f8db63",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To follow links on the World Wide Web in order to gather information."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internet"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c7933ed-871a-4c21-b513-162ddffb58e9",
                                                "sense_id": "a520a41d-ff81-3b11-8da4-ecdf877e7935",
                                                "text": "The online dictionary is regularly spidered by search engines."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
